eta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x-4x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+4x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3cb2fcb-3457-5a89-8968-6c0f2c2cfa83" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0097c7c0-21aa-5993-9c98-b4a1bd9f3827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)+\\frac{1}{32}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312698} {:answer/id #uuid "91d1c67e-e753-5392-b3f7-86f5d4678cbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)-\\frac{1}{32}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312699} {:answer/id #uuid "abb4d103-7f4d-5ba4-83a5-92691c37dbad" :answer/type {:db/ident :a