ng this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(19x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{38}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(19x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3cb2fcb-3457-5a89-8968-6c0f2c2cfa83" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25480d0a-de3e-5635-9b2e-aa7cfafe8da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{42}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(21x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312712} {:answer/id #uuid "be63231a-072c-5506-a300-1f1f99bc5015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{42}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(21x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312713} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5b71e7-ccb0-55ad-9cb1-647a968db5e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-\\frac{1}{42}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(21x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312714} {:answer/id #uuid "22d72adb-9ebe-5f2f-97b5-4c16eabd6f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{21}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(21x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312715} {:answer/id #uuid "82531663-165f-5955-b2ed-3443e7b2f9a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{13}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(13x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25480d0a-de3e-5635-9b2e-aa7cfafe8da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{42}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(21x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312712} :answer-field/id #uuid "584405eb-72a9-59c3-a0c3-f1b537689471" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b7ccbea5-2ae3-50dc-adb5-4a9e225a71a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340457" :question/problem "$\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x-8x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x+8x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(21x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(21x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+\\frac{1}{42}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(21x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312717 :knowledge-point/_questio