l gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)]}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2}))-\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(-1-0)-\\frac{1}{8}(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eee9ee8-c198-5308-b016-f88f3f990c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0eee9ee8-c198-5308-b016-f88f3f990c90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312754} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bae5a0-f5b6-58ee-97de-cd1c217b51fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fce53d9e-1d44-575e-8af4-56b946eb770f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340489" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x+3x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x-3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}(1-1)-\\frac{1}{12}(-1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db3928d-20ea-53fd-936a-f78657b52158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2db3928d-20ea-53fd-936a-f78657b52158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312757} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7a9d597-8dc0-56bf-ac1e-fc99d062081b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "937defff-0b54-5d84-8761-8f24a2d3bda2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340491" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x+x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186312758 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Product of Sine and Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191e24b8-1848-5c3c-bfa9-c7909dcbba7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312760} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f01ba5-3e32-5555-b13b-095531acef59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8f01ba5-3e32-5555-b13b-095531acef59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312761} :answer-field/id #uuid "19eee36c-9bd6-5baa-809d-d3073c43a866" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f1b9c1a-1da5-5dd5-bb7d-543d04c36f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-340492" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x+x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1)-\\frac{1}{12}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
